{"title":"2022 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 9","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Induction)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Induction)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5_(Combinatorics)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5 (Combinatorics)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_6_(Desperate)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 6 (Desperate)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Solution_7_(Partial_Fractions)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 7 (Partial Fractions)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Solution_8_(Taylor_Series)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 8 (Taylor Series)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Solution_9_(Really_Really_Fast_and_Cheesy)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 9 (Really Really Fast and Cheesy)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Interstigation\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">12</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Interstigation</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-13\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Ani_lytical\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">13</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Ani_lytical</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-14\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">14</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The sum\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/6/726b88e230d5c0a0303ef6ca7177fa73b7eec900.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{2!}+\\frac{2}{3!}+\\frac{3}{4!}+\\cdots+\\frac{2021}{2022!}\\]\" width=\"206\" height=\"37\" /> can be expressed as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/a/7fa5102d998ae15f75f5b7da238801da520cdedc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a-\\frac{1}{b!}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"51\" height=\"38\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> are positive integers. What is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/d/add2609af1bb7632cc22b68fd49fdd94de06b327.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"41\" height=\"16\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/7/097c57035c5c7bb6e61540c1eaff2321b79279cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 2020 \\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 2021 \\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 2022 \\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 2023 \\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 2024$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"487\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For all positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/4/c54e7152acd659788861f0453ac195c635e0a005.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"18\" height=\"13\" /> we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/4/504d797b74bd17ecef1a29dfdb0fa5c8f83127c5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{n}{(n+1)!}=\\frac{(n+1)-1}{(n+1)!}=\\frac{1}{n!}-\\frac{1}{(n+1)!}.\\]\" width=\"314\" height=\"43\" />\nNote that the original sum is a telescoping series:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/6/746d1c9eaa2537480946f87e42e06dcb8dc888ba.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} \\frac{1}{2!}+\\frac{2}{3!}+\\frac{3}{4!}+\\cdots+\\frac{2021}{2022!}  &amp;= \\left(\\frac{1}{1!}-\\frac{1}{2!}\\right)+\\left(\\frac{1}{2!}-\\frac{1}{3!}\\right)+\\left(\\frac{1}{3!}-\\frac{1}{4!}\\right)+\\cdots+\\left(\\frac{1}{2021!}-\\frac{1}{2022!}\\right) \\\\ &amp;= \\frac{1}{1!}+\\left(-\\frac{1}{2!}+\\frac{1}{2!}-\\frac{1}{3!}+\\frac{1}{3!}-\\frac{1}{4!}+\\cdots+\\frac{1}{2021!}\\right)-\\frac{1}{2022!} \\\\ &amp;= 1-\\frac{1}{2022!}. \\end{align*}\" width=\"731\" height=\"135\" />\nTherefore, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/4/6f46109e141fe0cc0c0c61c790b7613565228d06.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1+2022=\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}\\ 2023}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"181\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~mathboy100 ~MRENTHUSIASM\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We add <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/9/df91601ae54a1e5332021338a6537be000732ab0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2022!}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"47\" height=\"38\" /> to the original expression <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/5/ad521749a741d5009324c6088b8538c3fb56a187.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\left(\\frac{1}{2!}+\\frac{2}{3!}+\\frac{3}{4!}+\\cdots+\\frac{2021}{2022!}\\right)+\\frac{1}{2022!}=\\left(\\frac{1}{2!}+\\frac{2}{3!}+\\frac{3}{4!}+\\dots+\\frac{2020}{2021!}\\right)+\\frac{1}{2021!}.\\]\" width=\"615\" height=\"43\" />\nThis sum clearly telescopes, thus we end up with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/2/992faa4b4bb973257c17cb0170ba5b750ee4ad3f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(\\frac{1}{2!}+\\frac{2}{3!}\\right)+\\frac{1}{3!}=\\frac{2}{2!}=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"203\" height=\"45\" />. Thus the original expression is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/b/f9b340b9eb8fb0082f1ba15b865586e189249c6d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1-\\frac{1}{2022!}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"79\" height=\"38\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/4/19429e6c387ec6d992281084c5bbe0d76122f947.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1+2022=\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}\\ 2023}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"176\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~not_slay (+ minor LaTeX edit ~TaeKim)\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Induction.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Induction)\">Solution 3 (Induction)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Induction)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>By looking for a pattern, we see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/4/b34d3a90623052e21eb528a7e5bc15178bde09bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tfrac{1}{2!} = 1 - \\tfrac{1}{2!}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"86\" height=\"23\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/9/d0946b462148ca1672385ce82e3d7e47d29ed187.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tfrac{1}{2!} + \\tfrac{2}{3!} = \\tfrac{5}{6} = 1 - \\tfrac{1}{3!}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"158\" height=\"23\" />, so we can conclude by engineer's induction that the sum in the problem is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/9/579f392262758524a588c6d8b476faad44a9f12c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 - \\tfrac{1}{2022!}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"67\" height=\"23\" />, for an answer of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/f/32fad4b4faf57de6c514d3d4b7186d2bd0e32bbc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}\\ 2023}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"85\" height=\"30\" />. This can be proven with actual induction as well; we have already established <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> base cases, so now assume that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/1/1a1144708a7a0dc03882c253c7ef3ac82d77742a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tfrac{1}{2!} + \\tfrac{2}{3!} + \\cdots \\tfrac{n-1}{n!} = 1 - \\tfrac{1}{n!}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"200\" height=\"23\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/f/14f9a7f0a078b361958b8019646cc77aaac7ef78.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"47\" height=\"14\" />. For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/4/744cb4487683bf3d4bf277b31c61c149ad8f0216.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = k + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"78\" height=\"16\" /> we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/d/b4d69faca46b8a86f854ff753f1b6f760639232f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tfrac{1}{2!} + \\tfrac{2}{3!} + \\cdots \\tfrac{n-1}{n!} + \\tfrac{n}{(n+1)!} = 1 - \\tfrac{1}{n!} + \\tfrac{n}{(n+1)!} = 1 - \\tfrac{n+1}{(n+1)!} + \\tfrac{n}{(n+1)!} = 1 - \\tfrac{1}{(n+1)!}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"593\" height=\"26\" />, completing the proof.\n~eibc\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/027f0d227f3ec93e44a8dbec0b35a29d2e00529d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=\\frac{1}{1!}+\\frac{1}{2!}+\\frac{1}{3!}+\\dots+\\frac{1}{2022!}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"251\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/e/00e8f9762f8f99b423f9f37488c89fc27d5ad683.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} \\left(\\frac{1}{2!}+\\frac{2}{3!}+\\frac{3}{4!}+\\dots+\\frac{2021}{2022!}\\right)+\\left(\\frac{1}{1!}+\\frac{1}{2!}+\\frac{1}{3!}+\\dots+\\frac{1}{2022!}\\right)&amp;=\\frac{1}{1!}+\\frac{2}{2!}+\\frac{3}{3!}+\\dots+\\frac{2022}{2022!}\\\\ \\left(\\frac{1}{2!}+\\frac{2}{3!}+\\frac{3}{4!}+\\dots+\\frac{2021}{2022!}\\right)+x&amp;=\\frac{1}{0!}+\\frac{1}{1!}+\\frac{1}{2!}+\\dots+\\frac{1}{2021!}\\\\ \\left(\\frac{1}{2!}+\\frac{2}{3!}+\\frac{3}{4!}+\\dots+\\frac{2021}{2022!}\\right)+x&amp;=x+1-\\frac{1}{2022!}\\\\ \\left(\\frac{1}{2!}+\\frac{2}{3!}+\\frac{3}{4!}+\\dots+\\frac{2021}{2022!}\\right)&amp;=1-\\frac{1}{2022!}. \\end{align*}\" width=\"723\" height=\"191\" />\nTherefore, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/3/e939eaf3020454a450d3f4dac9c8c1f6d77a7aac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1+2022=\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) }2023}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"182\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~lopkiloinm\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_5_.28Combinatorics.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5_(Combinatorics)\">Solution 5 (Combinatorics)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5 (Combinatorics)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let's examine a tuple <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/3/fa35d9fc104207e09a712110ac81612c5b279a6c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sigma$\" width=\"10\" height=\"8\" /> containing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/b/0cb39dbc06a6cd0a0f4e4dd1e3ff461fb7026ba6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2022$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> distinct integers. We want to find the probability of the tuple being unsorted.\n</p><p>Suppose that we are looking at the first two items in our tuple. The probability of the first element being greater than the second element is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/b/3bb3cfc94b47cabab0fdb3f29a504350fa11a1eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2!}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"20\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>When we are looking at the first three items in our tuple, the probability of the second element being greater than the third element and the first element less than or equal to the second element is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/c/4bcc59ef34afc0501bca8bf808b130f907a88054.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2}{3!}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"20\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>Similarly, when we are looking at the first four items in our tuple, the probability of the third element being greater than the fourth element, the second element less than or equal to the third element, and the first element less than or equal to the second element is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/a/b1a79f90bf510cf10fe4820245c8f72c981afe7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3}{4!}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"20\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>More specifically, \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/5/d258f5f4b2a638ea9918db8318afa12d23a11016.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} \\bigcup_{n=2}^{2022}\\{\\sigma \\mid \\sigma_{n-1}&gt;\\sigma_n\\}&amp;=\\{\\sigma \\mid \\sigma_{1}&lt;\\sigma_{2}&lt;\\ldots&lt;\\sigma_{2022}\\}^\\complement\\\\ \\bigsqcup_{n=2}^{2022}\\{\\sigma \\mid \\sigma_{n-1}&gt;\\sigma_n, \\sigma_{n-2}\\leq\\sigma_{n-1},\\ldots, \\sigma_{1}\\leq\\sigma_{2}\\}&amp;=\\{\\sigma \\mid \\sigma_{1}&lt;\\sigma_{2}&lt;\\ldots&lt;\\sigma_{2022}\\}^\\complement\\\\ \\frac{\\#\\left(\\bigsqcup_{n=2}^{2022}\\{\\sigma \\mid \\sigma_{n-1}&gt;\\sigma_n, \\sigma_{n-2}\\leq\\sigma_{n-1},\\ldots, \\sigma_{1}\\leq\\sigma_{2}\\}\\right)}{\\#\\mathcal{S}}&amp;=\\frac{\\#\\left(\\{\\sigma \\mid \\sigma_{1}&lt;\\sigma_{2}&lt;\\ldots&lt;\\sigma_{2022}\\}^\\complement\\right)}{\\#\\mathcal{S}}\\\\ \\frac{\\sum_{n=2}^{2022}\\frac{2022!}{n!}(n-1)}{2022!}&amp;=\\frac{2022!-1}{2022!}\\\\ \\sum_{n=2}^{2022}\\frac{n-1}{n!}&amp;=1-\\frac{1}{2022!} \\end{align*}\" width=\"699\" height=\"282\" />\n</p><p>This series ends up being the probability of having the list unsorted and that is of course <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/b/f9b340b9eb8fb0082f1ba15b865586e189249c6d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1-\\frac{1}{2022!}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"79\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>~lopkiloinm\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_6_.28Desperate.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_6_(Desperate)\">Solution 6 (Desperate)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 6 (Desperate)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Because the fractions get smaller, it is obvious that the answer is less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, so we can safely assume that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/2/502e059d1a020b368aee3a99c5669d88331d321f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" /> (this can also be guessed by intuition using similar math problems). Looking at the answer choices, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/f/10f88b61648b206622c25b7f4ef0649f1a5030ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2018&lt;b&lt;2024$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"131\" height=\"15\" />. Because the last term consists of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/b/70b24df1eb41b2ddda78c8dbcc3bfc78d795b264.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2022!$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" /> (and the year was <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/b/0cb39dbc06a6cd0a0f4e4dd1e3ff461fb7026ba6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2022$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />) we can guess that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/b/92b8285b3c54bf957730107259731e32ed6c48d2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b=2022$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"70\" height=\"14\" />. Adding them yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/c/46cee368e9919280a67ce68f1531797b9e194b45.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1+2022=\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) }2023}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"177\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~iluvme and andy_lee\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_7_.28Partial_Fractions.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_7_(Partial_Fractions)\">Solution 7 (Partial Fractions)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 7 (Partial Fractions)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Knowing that the answer will be in the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/a/7fa5102d998ae15f75f5b7da238801da520cdedc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a-\\frac{1}{b!}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"51\" height=\"38\" />, we can guess that the sum telescopes. Using partial fractions, we can hope to rewrite <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/4/f0453d91d5a71361addc13ffb18d6efb432121de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{n-1}{n!}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"44\" height=\"37\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/6/a96933678b2e99f6460feb7a8e723b858609cb9a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{A}{(n-1)!}-\\frac{B}{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"108\" height=\"44\" />. Setting these equal and multiplying by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/f/63f344e7d8b14a7886fc7fb72da53cd0a3271dcc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n!$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/c/74c945393bb41d9046c4687ea1aafd0a79fb501c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n-1=An-B(n-1)!$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"191\" height=\"20\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/1/7f176663958e876e37afc7cfedf5adfebda08f2e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$An$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"26\" height=\"14\" /> is the only term with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> with degree <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, we can conclude that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/8/f18428217dcd07944b2adbebcafd0978587a770a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"46\" height=\"13\" />. This means that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/d/bbd5f2bba9250c9320755a706e8c8a2526d2379d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B=\\frac{1}{(n-1)!}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"106\" height=\"43\" />. Substituting, we find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/1/3c18a12f1108e0c813b4503dccce82219f60fadf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{n-1}{n!}=\\frac{1}{(n-1)!}-\\frac{1}{n!}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"180\" height=\"43\" />. This sum clearly telescopes and we obtain <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/b/f9b340b9eb8fb0082f1ba15b865586e189249c6d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1-\\frac{1}{2022!}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"79\" height=\"38\" />. This means that our desired answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/3/e939eaf3020454a450d3f4dac9c8c1f6d77a7aac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1+2022=\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) }2023}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"182\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~kn07\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_8_.28Taylor_Series.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_8_(Taylor_Series)\">Solution 8 (Taylor Series)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 8 (Taylor Series)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We calculate the Taylor series error to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/5/ab5d302db4a924f35664c8afc6a88b87465e6cf2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2023!}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"47\" height=\"38\" /> and this error happens <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/7/0873e9fed23538e535ac05c3284b86bd7bce6fd6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2023$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> times so it is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/3/ce36283661b3d5b3ebe5b20aa2a3c14b6ef447c8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2023}{2023!}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"47\" height=\"38\" /> which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/9/df91601ae54a1e5332021338a6537be000732ab0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2022!}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"47\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_9_.28Really_Really_Fast_and_Cheesy.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_9_(Really_Really_Fast_and_Cheesy)\">Solution 9 (Really Really Fast and Cheesy)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 9 (Really Really Fast and Cheesy)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Because this is obviously a telescoping series, we can guess small values and use engineer's induction. Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/d/ecd1683cf2a11900d584372f28f6d7da30871c74.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2!} = 1-\\frac{1}{2!}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"94\" height=\"38\" />, so we guess <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/2/502e059d1a020b368aee3a99c5669d88331d321f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/b/92b8285b3c54bf957730107259731e32ed6c48d2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b=2022$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"70\" height=\"14\" />. We get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/3/e939eaf3020454a450d3f4dac9c8c1f6d77a7aac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1+2022=\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) }2023}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"182\" height=\"30\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>by Ismail.maths\n<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=lt34QscjTf4&amp;list=PLmpPPbOoDfgj5BlPtEAGcB7BR_UA5FgFj\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=lt34QscjTf4&amp;list=PLmpPPbOoDfgj5BlPtEAGcB7BR_UA5FgFj</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Interstigation\">Video Solution by Interstigation</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Interstigation\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/_KNR0JV5rdI?t=1102\">https://youtu.be/_KNR0JV5rdI?t=1102</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Ani_lytical\">Video Solution by Ani_lytical</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=13\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Ani_lytical\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/P5n1I82IOvs?si=FoAcUvyNh-hIRyh7\">https://youtu.be/P5n1I82IOvs?si=FoAcUvyNh-hIRyh7</a>\n</p><p>~Ani_lytical\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=14\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10B\" title=\"2022 AMC 10B\">2022 AMC 10B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10B_Problems\" title=\"2022 AMC 10B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2022 AMC 10B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2022 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 8\">Problem 8</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2022 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 10\">Problem 10</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.ph